(Let's outline steps:)
(Initial state:)
(- candidate_created origin_availability_alpha, destination_availability_alpha, shift_candidate_alpha, shift_candidate_beta.)
(- candidate_prepared shift_candidate_alpha true.)
(- candidate_vehicle_linked: origin_availability_alpha -> vehicle_unit_alpha; destination_availability_alpha -> vehicle_unit_beta; shift_candidate_alpha -> vehicle_unit_gamma.)
(- vehicle_allocated for those three.)
(- cargo_available true.)
(- compliance_certificate linked to shift_candidate_alpha (so not available).)
(- dispatch_allocated shift_candidate_alpha true.)
(- dispatch_ready shift_candidate_alpha true.)
(- candidate_dispatch_slot_linked shift_candidate_alpha dispatch_slot_alpha.)
(- origin_availability_node_linked true, destination_availability_node_linked true.)
(- operator_available driver_operator_alpha.)
(- route_task_profile_available true.)
(- transport_leg_available true.)
(- equipment_available both.)
(- loading_container_available both.)
(- skill_certificate_available.)
(- etc.)
(Goal requires:)
(- candidate_prepared origin_availability_alpha (need to set))
(- candidate_prepared destination_availability_alpha)
(- candidate_task_profile_linked destination_availability_alpha route_task_profile_alpha)
(- compliance_certificate_available compliance_certificate_alpha (need to release from shift))
(- destination_availability_confirmed true)
(- destination_availability_locked true)
(- destination_node_occupied true)
(- destination_node_ready true)
(- dispatch_allocated origin_availability_alpha true)
(- dispatch_ready origin_availability_alpha true)
(- dispatch_ready destination_availability_alpha true)
(- dispatch_slot_available dispatch_slot_alpha true)
(- dispatched origin_availability_alpha true)
(- dispatched shift_candidate_alpha true)
(- origin_availability_confirmed true)
(- origin_availability_locked true)
(- origin_node_occupied true)
(- origin_node_ready true)
(- transport_leg_assembled true)
(- transport_leg_destination_linked transport_leg_alpha destination_node_alpha)
(- transport_leg_loading_authorized true)
(- transport_leg_origin_linked transport_leg_alpha origin_node_alpha)
(- vehicle_available vehicle_unit_alpha)
(- vehicle_available vehicle_unit_gamma)
(Now we need to ensure we don't accidentally lose any required predicates.)
(Let's design step-by-step.)
(We'll use variables: origin = origin_availability_alpha, dest = destination_availability_alpha, shift = shift_candidate_alpha, vehicle_origin = vehicle_unit_alpha, vehicle_dest = vehicle_unit_beta, vehicle_shift = vehicle_unit_gamma, dispatch_slot = dispatch_slot_alpha, operator = driver_operator_alpha, cargo = cargo_payload_alpha, route = route_task_profile_alpha, leg = transport_leg_alpha, comp = compliance_certificate_alpha, equip_alpha = equipment_resource_alpha, equip_beta = equipment_resource_beta, skill = skill_certificate_alpha, loading_cont_alpha = loading_container_alpha, loading_cont_beta = loading_container_beta, service_window_alpha, service_window_beta (not needed maybe).)
(Now steps:)
(1. Release compliance certificate from shift to make it available.)
(action: release_compliance_certificate shift_candidate_alpha compliance_certificate_alpha)
(Effect: compliance_certificate_available true, candidate_compliance_certificate_linked shift_candidate_alpha compliance_certificate_alpha removed.)
(2. Prepare origin:)
(Need to link task profile to origin, then prepare.)
(Action: attach_task_profile origin_availability_alpha route_task_profile_alpha)
(Precondition: candidate_created origin (true), vehicle_allocated origin (true), route_task_profile_available (true).)
(Effect: candidate_task_profile_linked origin route true, route_task_profile_available becomes false.)
(Then confirm_candidate_preparedness origin route_task_profile_alpha)
(Precondition: candidate_created origin, vehicle_allocated origin, candidate_task_profile_linked origin route, not candidate_prepared origin.)
(Effect: candidate_prepared origin true.)
(3. Prepare destination:)
(Since route_task_profile_available now false (due to origin link), we need to make it available again by detaching from origin? But we still need origin linked for later authorize. We could detach origin after preparing origin, but we need origin linked for authorize later. However we could prepare destination first using the profile, then detach destination, then link origin, prepare origin, use for authorize, then re-link destination for goal. Let's see.)
(Alternative: Prepare destination first using the profile, then detach destination, then link origin, prepare origin, use origin link for authorize, then detach origin, then link destination again for goal (destination already prepared). This seems workable.)
(Let's do:)
(Step A: attach_task_profile destination_availability_alpha route_task_profile_alpha)
(Step B: confirm_candidate_preparedness destination_availability_alpha route_task_profile_alpha)
(Step C: detach_task_profile destination_availability_alpha route_task_profile_alpha (makes profile available))
(Step D: attach_task_profile origin_availability_alpha route_task_profile_alpha)
(Step E: confirm_candidate_preparedness origin_availability_alpha route_task_profile_alpha)
(Now we have both prepared, origin linked, destination not linked (detached). We'll need destination linked for goal later; we can link after other steps.)
(But we also need destination linked for loading/unloading? Loading/unloading does not require task profile linked. So fine.)
(Now we need to load and unload payloads.)
(We have cargo_available true.)
(Load origin:)
(- load_origin_payload origin origin_node_alpha cargo_payload_alpha)
(Precondition: candidate_prepared origin (true after step E), origin_availability_node_linked origin origin_node_alpha (true), cargo_available true, not origin_availability_locked origin (currently false). Effect: origin_node_occupied true, origin_availability_locked true, origin_payload_linked origin cargo, cargo_available false.)
(Now unload origin:)
(- unload_origin_payload origin origin_node_alpha route_task_profile_alpha cargo_payload_alpha)
(Precondition: candidate_prepared origin (true), candidate_task_profile_linked origin route (true from step D), origin_availability_node_linked origin origin_node_alpha (true), origin_node_occupied origin (true after load), origin_payload_linked origin cargo (true), not origin_availability_confirmed origin (currently false? after load, origin_availability_locked true but not confirmed). Effect: origin_node_ready true, origin_availability_confirmed true, cargo_available true, not origin_payload_linked origin cargo.)
(Now origin has: occupied true (still true because effect didn't change), ready true, locked true (from load), confirmed true (from unload), cargo_available true, payload_linked false.)
(Now we need to load destination similarly.)
(Load destination:)
(- load_destination_payload destination destination_node_alpha cargo_payload_alpha)
(Precondition: candidate_prepared destination (true from step B), destination_availability_node_linked destination destination_node_alpha (true), cargo_available true (now true after unload origin), not destination_availability_locked destination (currently false). Effect: destination_node_occupied true, destination_availability_locked true, destination_payload_linked destination cargo, cargo_available false.)
(Unload destination:)
(- unload_destination_payload destination destination_node_alpha route_task_profile_alpha cargo_payload_alpha)
(Precondition: candidate_prepared destination (true), candidate_task_profile_linked destination route? Wait we detached destination's task profile earlier (step C). So candidate_task_profile_linked destination route is false. Unload requires candidate_task_profile_linked destination route. That's a problem. We need destination task profile linked for unload. So we cannot detach before unload.)
(Thus we need destination task profile linked for both load and unload. So we need to keep destination linked throughout loading/unloading steps. Similarly origin needs task profile linked for load and unload? Load origin does not require task profile linked. Unload origin requires candidate_task_profile_linked origin route (yes). So origin also needs task profile linked for unload. So both origin and destination need task profile linked for their respective unload actions. However we can perhaps use a different route_task_profile for each? Not available.)
(But maybe we can use the same route_task_profile for both, but we need it linked to both at same time for load/unload sequences. However we could load origin, unload origin (requires origin linked), then load destination (requires destination linked), then unload destination (requires destination linked). So we need origin linked during its load/unload, destination linked during its load/unload. They can be sequential: we can link origin, load origin, unload origin, detach origin; then link destination, load destination, unload destination, detach destination; then later link destination again for goal. That works because after unloading origin, we detach origin (making profile available) then link destination.)
(Thus we need to keep task profile linked for each during its load/unload pair.)
(Thus plan:)
(- Link origin, prepare origin.)
(- Load origin, unload origin.)
(- Detach origin (optional after unload).)
(- Link destination, prepare destination.)
(- Load destination, unload destination.)
(- Detach destination (optional).)
(- Later link destination for goal (need to have it linked at end). We'll link destination after all other steps, before goal.)
(Now we also need to authorize transport leg loading, which requires origin_availability_locked and candidate_task_profile_linked origin route. So after we have origin locked and confirmed, we need origin linked for authorize. So we must keep origin linked at least until after authorize. After authorize, we can detach origin if we want.)
(Thus we need origin linked during: prepare, load origin, unload origin, lock origin? Lock does not require task profile linked. Authorize requires origin linked. So we need origin linked at least until after authorize. After that we can detach.)
(Thus steps:)
(- Link origin, prepare origin.)
(- Load origin.)
(- Unload origin.)
(- (Now origin has occupied&ready, locked? not yet locked.))
(- Lock origin (requires candidate_prepared, candidate_operator_linked, origin_node_ready, origin_availability_node_linked, not origin_availability_locked). We'll need operator linked.)
(- After lock, we have origin_availability_locked true, origin_availability_confirmed true.)
(- Then authorize transport leg loading (requires origin_availability_locked, candidate_task_profile_linked origin route, transport_leg_assembled? Wait authorize requires transport_leg_assembled? Actually authorize_transport_leg_loading precondition: (transport_leg_assembled ?transport_leg) (origin_availability_locked ?origin_availability) (candidate_task_profile_linked ?origin_availability ?route_task_profile) (not transport_leg_loading_authorized ?transport_leg). So we need transport_leg_assembled before authorize. So we need to assemble transport leg before authorize. However assemble_transport_leg requires origin_availability_locked and destination_availability_locked and nodes ready and availabilities confirmed. So we need destination also locked before we can assemble. So we need to lock destination first (or at least have destination locked) before assembling.)
(Thus we need to lock both origin and destination before assembling leg.)
(Thus we need to lock origin and destination (both require candidate_prepared, candidate_operator_linked, node_ready, etc). For locking we need operator linked. We'll need to assign operator to each.)
(Thus we need to have origin and destination both prepared, and we need to have operator assigned to each for locking.)
(We can assign operator to origin, lock origin, release operator, assign operator to destination, lock destination, release operator.)
(Now after both locked, we can assemble transport leg (requires both locked, nodes ready, availabilities confirmed, transport_leg_available). Nodes ready we have after unload (origin_node_ready true, destination_node_ready true). Availabilities confirmed we have from lock. Good.)
(After assemble, we need authorize transport leg loading, which requires origin_availability_locked (we have), candidate_task_profile_linked origin route (we need origin linked at this time). So we must keep origin linked through lock and assemble and authorize.)
(Thus we must not detach origin before authorize.)
(Thus we need to keep origin linked from prepare through lock, assemble, authorize. After authorize, we can detach origin if we want.)
(Destination does not need to be linked for authorize, but we need destination linked for goal at end. So we can keep destination linked after preparing, through load/unload, lock, etc., and keep it linked for goal.)
(Thus we need to keep destination linked from prepare through load/unload, lock, etc., and keep it linked at end.)
(Thus we cannot detach destination until after goal (or we can detach and relink later but need it linked at goal). Simpler: keep destination linked throughout.)
(Now we need to manage the single route_task_profile resource: we cannot have both origin and destination linked simultaneously. But we need origin linked for authorize, and destination linked for goal (and also for load/unload etc). However we could detach destination after its load/unload and lock, then later re-link it for goal after we are done with origin's authorize. Since after authorize we no longer need origin linked? Actually after authorize we still need origin linked? Not for any further goal predicate. Goal does not require origin linked. So we can detach origin after authorize, freeing the profile, then link destination for goal.)
(Thus sequence:)
(- Link origin, prepare origin.)
(- Load origin, unload origin.)
(- Lock origin (requires operator linked).)
(- (Keep origin linked))
(- Prepare destination? We'll need destination prepared before lock. So we need to prepare destination earlier, but we cannot have both linked at same time. So we need to prepare destination while origin not linked (or after we detach origin). But we need origin locked before we can assemble leg, which requires destination locked as well. So we need both locked before assemble. So we need to have destination prepared and linked (for its load/unload) before we lock origin? Actually we can prepare destination, load/unload, lock destination, then detach destination (freeing profile), then link origin, prepare origin, load/unload, lock origin, then we have both locked but neither linked. Then we need origin linked for authorize, so we link origin again (but it's already prepared and locked; linking does not require candidate_prepared? attach_task_profile requires candidate_created and vehicle_allocated and route_task_profile_available. It does not require candidate_prepared. So we can link origin even if already prepared and locked. Good. So we can link origin after it's locked, as long as route_task_profile_available is free. Then we can authorize.)
(Thus we can detach destination after its lock, making profile free, then link origin, prepare origin (if not already prepared), load/unload origin, lock origin (but origin already locked? we need to lock origin after its load/unload; we can lock origin after linking). However we need origin locked for authorize; we can lock origin after linking.)
(Thus overall plan:)
(Phase A: Prepare destination, load/unload, lock destination, then detach destination (free profile).)
(Phase B: Prepare origin, load/unload, lock origin, then link origin (if not already linked) for authorize, authorize leg loading, assemble leg? Wait assemble leg needs both locked before authorize? Actually authorize requires transport_leg_assembled. So we need to assemble leg before authorize. So we need to have leg assembled before authorize. Assemble leg requires both locked and nodes ready and availabilities confirmed. So we need to have both origin and destination locked before assembling. So we must lock both before assembling. So we need to lock origin and destination before assemble. Thus we need to have both locked while profile is free (since we cannot have both linked). That's okay: lock does not require task profile linked. So we can lock origin and destination without having them linked. Good.)
(Thus we can:)
(- Prepare destination, load/unload, lock destination (no need for task profile linked during lock).)
(- Detach destination (free profile).)
(- Prepare origin, load/unload, lock origin.)
(- Now both origin and destination are locked, profile free.)
(- Assemble transport leg (requires both locked, nodes ready, availabilities confirmed, transport_leg_available). Nodes ready we have from unload steps. Availabilities confirmed we have from lock. Good.)
(- Now we need to authorize transport leg loading: requires origin_availability_locked (true), candidate_task_profile_linked origin route (so we need to link origin now), transport_leg_assembled (true), not transport_leg_loading_authorized.)
(- So we link origin (attach_task_profile origin route). Note origin already prepared and locked; attach_task_profile only needs candidate_created, vehicle_allocated, route_task_profile_available (which is free now). Good.)
(- Then authorize_transport_leg_loading leg origin route.)
(- After authorize, we can detach origin if we want (not needed for goal). But we need destination linked for goal. So we need to link destination again (attach_task_profile destination route) after we detach origin to free profile.)
(- Then we have destination linked (goal requires). Also we need destination prepared (already true). Good.)
(- Then we need to set dispatch_ready for origin and destination via mark_*_dispatch_ready actions. Those require origin_availability_locked, origin_availability_confirmed, transport_leg_assembled, transport_leg_loading_authorized, not dispatch_ready. We have all that after authorize.)
(- So we can run mark_origin_availability_dispatch_ready origin leg, and mark_destination_availability_dispatch_ready destination leg.)
(- Then allocate dispatch slot to origin: allocate_dispatch_slot_for_candidate origin dispatch_slot_alpha route_task_profile_alpha? Wait allocate_dispatch_slot_for_candidate requires candidate_task_profile_linked ?candidate ?route_task_profile. So we need origin linked to route task profile for allocation. We have origin linked currently (we just linked for authorize). We could keep it linked or re-link after detach. We'll keep origin linked for allocation.)
(- Precondition: dispatch_ready origin (we will set after mark), candidate_task_profile_linked origin route, dispatch_slot_available slot (currently? after releasing shift? We'll need to make slot available). We'll handle slot later.)
(- Effect: dispatch_allocated origin true, candidate_dispatch_slot_linked origin slot, not dispatch_slot_available slot.)
(- Then execute_origin_dispatch origin vehicle_unit_alpha dispatch_slot_alpha: requires dispatch_allocated origin, candidate_vehicle_linked origin vehicle_unit_alpha (true), candidate_dispatch_slot_linked origin slot, not dispatched origin. Effect: dispatched origin true, vehicle_available vehicle_unit_alpha, dispatch_slot_available slot true.)
(- Now slot available again.)
