(Now we need to ensure we don't inadvertently lose any needed predicates via actions that have negative effects.)
(Let's list actions and their negative effects:)
(- release_compliance_certificate: removes candidate_compliance_certificate_linked shift compliance, adds compliance_certificate_available. Good.)
(- attach_task_profile: adds candidate_task_profile_linked, removes route_task_profile_available.)
(- confirm_candidate_preparedness: adds candidate_prepared (no negative).)
(- detach_task_profile: removes candidate_task_profile_linked, adds route_task_profile_available.)
(- load_origin_payload: adds origin_node_occupied, origin_availability_locked, origin_payload_linked, removes cargo_available.)
(- unload_origin_payload: adds origin_node_ready, origin_availability_confirmed, cargo_available, removes origin_payload_linked.)
(- load_destination_payload: adds destination_node_occupied, destination_availability_locked, destination_payload_linked, removes cargo_available.)
(- unload_destination_payload: adds destination_node_ready, destination_availability_confirmed, cargo_available, removes destination_payload_linked.)
(- allocate_dispatch_slot_for_candidate: adds dispatch_allocated ?candidate, candidate_dispatch_slot_linked ?candidate ?dispatch_slot, removes dispatch_slot_available ?dispatch_slot.)
(- execute_origin_dispatch: adds dispatched ?origin_availability, vehicle_available ?vehicle_unit, dispatch_slot_available ?dispatch_slot. (No negative effects on other predicates.))
(- execute_schedule_dispatch: adds dispatched ?candidate, vehicle_available ?vehicle_unit, dispatch_slot_available ?dispatch_slot.)
(- mark_origin_availability_dispatch_ready: adds dispatch_ready ?origin_availability (no negative).)
(- mark_destination_availability_dispatch_ready: adds dispatch_ready ?destination_availability.)
(- lock_origin_availability: adds origin_availability_locked, origin_availability_confirmed (no negative).)
(- lock_destination_availability: adds destination_availability_locked, destination_availability_confirmed.)
(- activate_origin_node: adds origin_node_ready (no negative). Not needed if already ready.)
(- activate_destination_node: adds destination_node_ready.)
(- assemble_transport_leg: adds transport_leg_assembled, transport_leg_origin_linked, transport_leg_destination_linked, removes transport_leg_available.)
(- authorize_transport_leg_loading: adds transport_leg_loading_authorized (no negative).)
(Now we need to ensure we don't accidentally lose needed predicates like candidate_prepared (none of actions remove it). Good.)
(Now we need to ensure we have vehicle_available for origin and destination vehicles after dispatch. The execute_*_dispatch actions add vehicle_available for the vehicle used. They do not remove any vehicle_available elsewhere. So fine.)
(Now we need to ensure we have dispatch_slot_available at end. We'll have after origin dispatch.)
(Now we need to ensure we have candidate_dispatch_slot_linked origin dispatch_slot_alpha (from allocate). After origin dispatch, does execute_origin_dispatch affect candidate_dispatch_slot_linked? No. So remains true.)
(Now we need to ensure we have cargo_available? Not required.)
(Now we need to ensure we have origin_availability_locked true after lock origin; we will not unlock it anywhere. No action removes origin_availability_locked except? There is no action to unlock. So stays true.)
(Similarly destination_availability_locked stays true.)
(Now we need to ensure origin_availability_confirmed true after lock origin and unload origin? Actually lock adds origin_availability_confirmed true. Unload origin also adds origin_availability_confirmed true (but it's already true). So fine.)
(Destination similarly.)
