(Now we need to ensure we have operator assigned to origin and destination for locking. We'll use assign_operator_resource and release_operator_resource.)
(Action assign_operator_resource: precondition candidate_prepared ?candidate, operator_available ?operator. Effect: candidate_operator_linked ?candidate ?operator, not operator_available ?operator.)
(Release_operator_resource: precondition candidate_operator_linked ?candidate ?operator. Effect: operator_available ?operator, not candidate_operator_linked ?candidate ?operator.)
(Thus we need to assign operator to origin, lock origin, release operator, assign operator to destination, lock destination, release operator.)
(We must ensure operator_available is true initially (yes). After assigning to origin, operator becomes unavailable. After releasing, becomes available again. Then assign to destination, lock, release.)
